paragraphs.analysis:
if · true · man(pl.) · you(pol./pl.)(pl.) · be(prs.), · of · your-brother(pl.) · one · in · your-prison-house · bind(pass.,opt.). · you(pol./pl.)(pl.) · go(imp.), · for · your-house:pl-famine · corn(acc.) · carry(imp.),
Analysis: if true man:pl you:pl be:pr, of your/brother:pl unta_cardinal_b_over_b in your/prison/house bind:psv:opt. you:pl go:imp, for your/house:pl/kjv_famine corn:a carry:imp,
This revises the earlier arrangement: one is held, the others travel. The plurality of their households is retained despite the larger shared kin-house.

if · with · we(pl.) · our(sg.whole.)-brother(acc.) · you(fam.sg.) · send(fut.), · down · we(pl.) · go(fut.) · and · to · you(fam.sg.) · food(acc.) · buy(fut.),
Analysis: if with wepl ourone/brother:a thou send:fu, down wepl go:fu and to thou food:a buy:fu,
Shared kinship uses our-one, while the travelers remain a plural party undertaking the journey.

for · he(sg.) · surety · I(sg.) · be(fut.). · of · my-hand · he(sg.)(acc.) · you(fam.sg.) · require(fut.). · if · to · you(fam.sg.) · he(sg.)(acc.) · I(sg.) · bring(prs.) · not · and · before · you(fam.sg.) · he(sg.)(acc.) · set(prs.) · not, · then · forever · blame(acc.) · I(sg.) · carry(opt.),
Analysis: for he surety i be:fu. of my/hand he:a thou require:fu. if to thou he:a i bring:pr not and before thou he:a set:pr not, then forever blame:a i carry:opt,
Judah's guarantee is personal singular-I and enduring liability, distinct from Reuben's offer to kill two sons. Bear blame uses carry, not the beget sense of bear.

if(unmarked.continuation) · they(pl.)(acc.) · go(inf.) · let(inf.) · you(fam.sg.) · refuse(prs.), · behold · with · frog(pl.) · all · thy-land-edge(pl.,acc.) · I(pl.self.) · strike(fut.),
Analysis: if:cont they:a go:inf let:inf thou refuse:pr, behold with kjv_frog:pl all thy/land/edge:pl:a ipl strike:fu,
The threatened instrument is frogs, not a new military force. Borders retain the territorial image rather than being restricted to a thin boundary line. Historical correction 281: clause-cont. Participant identities, polarity and quantities retained.

for · if · they(pl.)(acc.) · go(inf.) · let(inf.) · you(fam.sg.) · refuse(prs.) · and · still · they(pl.)(acc.) · hold(inf.) · will(prs.),
Analysis: for if they:a go:inf let:inf thou refuse:pr and still they:a hold:inf will:pr,
Will means intention to continue holding them, not a separate future tense added mechanically from English.

for · six · day(pl.) · you(fam.sg.) · labour(fut.) · and · all · thy-work(acc.) · do(fut.),
Analysis: for unta_cardinal_g_over_b day:pl thou labour:fu and all thy/work:a do:fu,
The six-day clause is retained before the seventh-day prohibition rather than reducing the passage to only the rest rule.

if(unmarked.continuation) · servant(nom.) · plainly · say(fut.): · my-master(acc.), · my-wife(acc.) · and · my-child(pl.,acc.) · I(sg.) · love(prs.), · free · I(sg.) · go(fut.) · not · out,
Analysis: if:cont servant:n plainly say:fu: my/master:a, my/wife:a and my/child:pl:a i love:pr, free i go:fu not out,
This is the servant's personal-I declaration under the preceding family constraint. It is not recast as a sovereign household plural-I or certified as uncoerced consent. Historical correction 281: clause-cont. Participant identities, polarity and quantities retained.

if(unmarked.continuation) · man(pl.,nom.) · together · strive(prs.) · and · one(nom.) · another(acc.) · with · stone · or · with · his-fist · strike(prs.) · and · he(sg.) · die(prs.) · not · but · his-bed(acc.) · keep(prs.),
Analysis: if:cont man:pl:n together strive:pr and unta_cardinal_b_over_b:n another:a with stone or with his/fist strike:pr and he die:pr not but his/bed:a keep:pr,
Stone and fist are alternative instruments. Bed-keeping is incapacity rather than guarding a piece of furniture. Historical correction 281: clause-cont. Participant identities, polarity and quantities retained.

if(unmarked.continuation) · any · harm(nom.) · follow(prs.), · then · life(acc.) · for · life · you(fam.sg.) · give(fut.),
Analysis: if:cont any harm:n follow:pr, then life:a for life thou give:fu,
The condition continues the preceding case. No modern legal interpretation of proportional compensation versus bodily retaliation is inserted as if explicit in this verse. Historical correction 281: clause-cont. Participant identities, polarity and quantities retained.

if · in · any · way · they(pl.)(acc.) · you(fam.sg.) · afflict(prs.) · and · to · I(pl.self.) · at · all · they(pl.) · cry(prs.), · surely · their-cry(nmlz.,acc.) · I(pl.self.) · hear(fut.),
Analysis: if in any way they:a thou kjv_afflict:pr and to ipl at all they cry:pr, surely their/cry:ev:a ipl hear:fu,
The divine listener uses plural-I, while vulnerable people remain distinct callers. The emphatic at-all and surely retain the source's force.

if · at · all · as · pledge · thy-neighbour-clothing(acc.) · you(fam.sg.) · take(prs.), · by · when · sun(nom.) · go(prs.) · down · to · he(sg.) · it(acc.) · you(fam.sg.) · deliver(fut.),
Analysis: if at all as pledge thy/neighbour/clothing:a thou take:pr, by when sun:n go:pr down to he it:a thou deliver:fu,
Security-taking and the deadline for return are both explicit. The garment is not replaced by a generic monetary asset.

for(unmarked.continuation) · six · year(pl.) · thy-land(acc.) · you(fam.sg.) · sow(fut.) · and · of · it · fruit(pl.,acc.) · gather(fut.) · in,
Analysis: for:cont unta_cardinal_g_over_b year:pl thy/land:a thou kjv_sow:fu and of it fruit:pl:a gather:fu in,
The duration concerns agricultural years, distinct from the six-day work cycle restated below. Historical correction 281: clause-cont. Participant identities, polarity and quantities retained.

for · there · their-hand(pl.,acc.) · and · their-foot(pl.,acc.) · Aaron · and · his-son(pl.,nom.) · wash(fut.),
Analysis: for there their/hand:pl:a and their/foot:pl:a kjv_aaron and his/son:pl:n wash:fu,
The specified body parts are hands and feet, not a repeated full-body washing inferred from the consecration rite.

for · no · other · god{above-owner}(acc.) · you(fam.sg.) · worship(fut.), · for · LORD{name-lord} · whose · name · Jealous · be(prs.) · jealous · god{above-owner} · be(prs.),
Analysis: for no other kjv_god:a thou kjv_worship:fu, for kjv_lord whose name kjv_jealous_name be:pr jealous kjv_god be:pr,
Jealous as expressly named title receives a separate proper-name role, tied to the adjective without replacing the deity with a modern psychiatric description.

if(unmarked.continuation) · in · skin · leprosy{source}(nom.) · wide(adv.) · break(prs.) · out · and · of · he(sg.) · who · plague(acc.) · have(prs.) · all · skin(acc.) · leprosy{source}(nom.) · cover(prs.) · from · his-head · even · to · his-foot · wherever · priest(nom.) · look(prs.),
Analysis: if:cont in skin kjv_leprosy:n wide:adv break:pr out and of he who plague:a have:pr all skin:a kjv_leprosy:n cover:pr from his/head even to his/foot wherever priest:n look:pr,
Whole coverage is a distinct condition whose counterintuitive consequence is retained in the next verse. Historical correction 281: clause-cont. Participant identities, polarity and quantities retained.

if · man · or · woman · upon · head · or · beard · plague(acc.) · have(prs.),
Analysis: if man or woman upon head or beard plague:a have:pr,
Both sexes are included in the supplied conditional; beard does not erase the woman alternative.

if · also · man · or · woman · in · of · their-flesh · skin · bright{skin} · spot(pl.,acc.) · have(prs.) · even · white · bright{skin} · spot(pl.),
Analysis: if also man or woman in of their/flesh skin kjv_bright_skin spot:pl:a have:pr even white kjv_bright_skin spot:pl,
A further case is introduced, not assumed to be leprosy merely because it is a visible mark.

if(additive.clause) · in · garment · or · in · skin · either · in · warp{cloth} · or · in · woof{cloth} · or · in · any · thing · of · skin · plague · somewhat · green · or · somewhat · red · be(prs.), · of · leprosy{source} · plague · it · be(prs.) · and · to · priest · show(pass.,fut.),
Analysis: if:add in garment or in skin either in kjv_warp_thread or in kjv_woof_thread or in any thing of skin plague somewhat green or somewhat red be:pr, of kjv_leprosy plague it be:pr and to priest show:psv:fu,
The source's colors and materials remain without confidently naming a modern fungus or chemical cause. Historical correction 281: clause-add. Participant identities, polarity and quantities retained.

if(unmarked.continuation) · priest(nom.) · look(fut.) · and · behold · plague · in · garment · either · in · warp{cloth} · or · in · woof{cloth} · or · in · any · thing · of · skin · spread(prs.pf.) · not,
Analysis: if:cont priest:n look:fu and behold plague in garment either in kjv_warp_thread or in kjv_woof_thread or in any thing of skin spread:perf not,
This introduces a separate washing-and-observation branch, not an immediate clean judgment. Historical correction 281: clause-cont. Participant identities, polarity and quantities retained.

if(unmarked.continuation) · priest(nom.) · look(prs.) · and · behold · plague · somewhat · dark · after · of · it · wash(nmlz.) · be(prs.), · then · out · of · garment · or · out · of · skin · or · out · of · warp{cloth} · or · out · of · woof{cloth} · it(acc.) · he(sg.) · rend(fut.),
Analysis: if:cont priest:n look:pr and behold plague somewhat dark after of it wash:ev be:pr, then out of garment or out of skin or out of kjv_warp_thread or out of kjv_woof_thread it:a he rend:fu,
Rend removes material; the inherited tear noun for an eye-drop would be wrong here. Historical correction 281: clause-cont. Participant identities, polarity and quantities retained.

if(unmarked.continuation) · plague(nom.) · again · come(prs.) · and · in · house · break(prs.) · out · after · stone(pl.,acc.) · he(sg.) · take(prs.pf.) · away · and · after · house(acc.) · he(sg.) · scrape(prs.pf.) · and · after · it · plaster{apply}(pass.,prs.pf.),
Analysis: if:cont plague:n again come:pr and in house break:pr out after stone:pl:a he take:perf away and after house:a he kjv_scrape:perf and after it kjv_plaster_apply:psv:perf,
Recurrence is tested after the full sequence, not merely after any one action. Historical correction 281: clause-cont. Participant identities, polarity and quantities retained.

if(unmarked.continuation) · of · land · people(nom.) · in · any · manner · their-eye(pl.,acc.) · from · man · hide(prs.) · when · of · his-seed{descendants} · to · Molech · he(sg.) · give(prs.) · and · he(sg.)(acc.) · kill(prs.) · not,
Analysis: if:cont of land people:n in any manner their/eye:pl:a from man hide:pr when of his/kjv_seedline to kjv_molech he give:pr and he:a kill:pr not,
The concealment and failure to impose the prescribed penalty are both retained, not reduced to private disagreement. Historical correction 281: clause-cont. Participant identities, polarity and quantities retained.

for · whatever · man · who · blemish(acc.) · have(prs.) · he(sg.) · be(prs.), · he(sg.) · approach(fut.) · not: · blind · man · or · lame · or · he(sg.) · who · flat · nose(acc.) · have(prs.) · or · any · thing · beyond · need,
Analysis: for whatever man who kjv_blemish:a have:pr he be:pr, he approach:fu not: blind man or kjv_lame or he who flat nose:a have:pr or any thing beyond need,
Superfluous is kept as the source's unspecified bodily excess, not assigned a modern diagnostic category or an extra moral meaning.

if(unmarked.continuation) · man(nom.) · in · his-neighbour · blemish(acc.) · cause(prs.), · as · he(sg.) · do(prs.pf.) · so · to · he(sg.) · it · do(pass.,fut.),
Analysis: if:cont man:n in his/neighbour kjv_blemish:a cause:pr, as he do:perf so to he it do:psv:fu,
The passive retaliation formula remains bodily and reciprocal, without a silently substituted financial payment. Historical correction 281: clause-cont. Participant identities, polarity and quantities retained.

if(unmarked.continuation) · you(pol./pl.)(pl.) · say(fut.): · what(acc.) · in · seventh · year · we(sg.whole.) · eat(fut.)? · behold, · we(sg.whole.) · sow(fut.) · not · nor · our(sg.whole.)-increase(acc.) · gather(fut.) · in,
Analysis: if:cont you:pl say:fu: what:a in unta_ordinal_h_over_b year wesg eat:fu? behold, wesg kjv_sow:fu not nor ourone/increase:a gather:fu in,
The imagined community speaks as a single dependent whole. Singular-we contrasts with the divine plural-I response, without claiming the humans literally have one stomach. Historical correction 281: clause-cont. Participant identities, polarity and quantities retained.

if(unmarked.continuation) · man(nom.) · none · to · it(acc.) · redeem(inf.) · have(prs.) · and · himself · it(acc.) · redeem(inf.) · can(prs.),
Analysis: if:cont man:n none to it:a redeem:inf have:pr and himself it:a redeem:inf can:pr,
The second condition allows self-financed recovery after absence of a kin redeemer; neither condition is omitted. Historical correction 281: clause-cont. Participant identities, polarity and quantities retained.

if · in · my(pl.self.)-statute(pl.) · you(pol./pl.)(pl.) · walk(prs.) · and · my(pl.self.)-command(pl.,acc.) · keep(prs.) · and · they(pl.)(acc.) · do(prs.),
Analysis: if in mypl/kjv_statute:pl you:pl walk:pr and mypl/command:pl:a keep:pr and they:a do:pr,
This is the condition for the following promises, not an assertion that obedience has already occurred.

if(unmarked.continuation) · by · these · thing(pl.) · by · I(pl.self.) · you(pol./pl.)(pl.) · reform{discipline}(pass.,inf.) · will(prs.) · not · but · contrary · to · I(pl.self.) · walk(inf.) · will(prs.),
Analysis: if:cont by these thing:pl by ipl you:pl kjv_reform_discipline:psv:inf will:pr not but contrary to ipl walk:inf will:pr,
Reformed is correction through the threatened discipline, not a modern religious movement or an architectural reshaping. Historical correction 281: clause-cont. Participant identities, polarity and quantities retained.

if(unmarked.continuation) · for · all · this · to · I(pl.self.) · you(pol./pl.)(pl.) · listen(inf.) · will(prs.) · not · but · contrary · to · I(pl.self.) · walk(prs.),
Analysis: if:cont for all this to ipl you:pl listen:inf will:pr not but contrary to ipl walk:pr,
The repeated conditional continues the escalating sequence instead of declaring a wholly new unrelated event. Historical correction 281: clause-cont. Participant identities, polarity and quantities retained.

if · their-iniquity · and · of · their-father(pl.) · iniquity(acc.) · they(pl.) · confess(fut.) · with · their-trespass · which · against · I(pl.self.) · they(pl.) · trespass(pst.) · and · that · also · contrary · to · I(pl.self.) · they(pl.) · walk(prs.pf.),
Analysis: if their/kjv_iniquity and of their/father:pl kjv_iniquity:a they confess:fu with their/kjv_trespass which against ipl they kjv_trespass:pa and that also contrary to ipl they walk:perf,
The confession includes ancestral wrongdoing and the community's own acts; neither substitutes for the other.

if(unmarked.continuation) · any · unclean{ritual} · beast · of · which · to · LORD{name-lord} · sacrifice{cut-gift}(acc.) · they(pl.) · offer(prs.) · not · it · be(prs.) · then · beast(acc.) · before · priest · he(sg.) · present(fut.),
Analysis: if:cont any kjv_unclean_ritual beast of which to kjv_lord kjv_sacrifice:a they offer:pr not it be:pr then beast:a before priest he present:fu,
Unclean is the inherited ritual category, not dirtiness removable by ordinary washing. Historical correction 281: clause-cont. Participant identities, polarity and quantities retained.

if(unmarked.continuation) · to · LORD{name-lord} · field(acc.) · which · he(sg.) · buy(prs.pf.) · which · his-possession{own-state}(rel.chain.2) · field(pl.) · be(prs.) · not · man(nom.) · sanctify(prs.),
Analysis: if:cont to kjv_lord field:a which he buy:perf which his/kjv_possession:relpair field:pl be:pr not man:n sanctify:pr,
Purchased holding is distinguished from possession-land before its different return rule. Historical correction 281: relational-clitic-2, clause-cont. Participant identities, polarity and quantities retained.

for · to · Moses · LORD{name-lord}(nom.) · speak(prs.pf.) · say(cv.),
Analysis: for to kjv_moses kjv_lord:n speak:perf say:cv,
The explanation looks back to prior instruction rather than inserting a new count before the order.

from · 30 · year(pl.) · old · and · up · even · to · 50 · year(pl.) · old, · each · one(person) · who · into · service · enter(prs.) · for · work · in · of · congregation · tabernacle,
Analysis: from unta_cardinal_da_over_b year:pl old and up even to unta_cardinal_fa_over_b year:pl old, each one who into service enter:pr for work in of kjv_congregation kjv_tabernacle,
The stated inclusion criterion remains attached to the following total.

from · 30 · year(pl.) · old · and · up · even · to · 50 · year(pl.) · old, · each · one(person) · who · into · service · enter(prs.) · for · work · in · of · congregation · tabernacle,
Analysis: from unta_cardinal_da_over_b year:pl old and up even to unta_cardinal_fa_over_b year:pl old, each one who into service enter:pr for work in of kjv_congregation kjv_tabernacle,
The age window remains inclusive as the source describes it, without an invented retirement calculation.

from · 30 · year(pl.) · old · and · up · even · to · 50 · year(pl.) · old, · each · one(person) · who · into · service · enter(prs.) · for · work · in · of · congregation · tabernacle,
Analysis: from unta_cardinal_da_over_b year:pl old and up even to unta_cardinal_fa_over_b year:pl old, each one who into service enter:pr for work in of kjv_congregation kjv_tabernacle,
This repeated criterion is not shortened away from the verse-level translation.

from · 30 · year(pl.) · old · and · up · even · to · 50 · year(pl.) · old, · each · one(person) · who · come(pst.) · to · of · serve(nmlz.) · service · and · of · burden · service(acc.) · in · of · congregation · tabernacle · do(inf.),
Analysis: from unta_cardinal_da_over_b year:pl old and up even to unta_cardinal_fa_over_b year:pl old, each one who come:pa to of serve:ev service and of burden service:a in of kjv_congregation kjv_tabernacle do:inf,
The double service expression deliberately preserves the source's cumbersome distinction.

from(additive.clause) · of · 50 · year(pl.) · age · to · its-service(acc.) · attend(inf.) · they(pl.) · cease(fut.) · and · no · more · serve(fut.),
Analysis: from:add of unta_cardinal_fa_over_b year:pl age to its/service:a attend:inf they cease:fu and no more serve:fu,
The next verse still permits a related assisting role; both statements are preserved. Historical correction 281: clause-add. Participant identities, polarity and quantities retained.

if(unmarked.continuation) · you(pol./pl.)(pl.) · err(prs.pf.) · and · all · these · command(pl.,acc.) · which · to · Moses · LORD{name-lord}(nom.) · speak(prs.pf.) · observe(prs.pf.) · not,
Analysis: if:cont you:pl err:perf and all these command:pl:a which to kjv_moses kjv_lord:n speak:perf observe:perf not,
Error and failure to observe introduce the ignorance condition continued below. Historical correction 281: clause-cont. Participant identities, polarity and quantities retained.

if · woman · also · vow(acc.) · to · LORD{name-lord} · vow(prs.) · and · herself(acc.) · by · bond · bind(prs.), · in · of · her-father · house · in · her-youth · be(cv.),
Analysis: if woman also vow:a to kjv_lord vow:pr and herself:a by bond bind:pr, in of her/father house in her/youth be:cv,
Conditional domestic status is retained; this is not a universal rule for all women regardless of household.

if(unmarked.continuation) · she(sg.) · at · all · husband · have(pst.) · when · she(sg.) · vow(pst.) · or · from · her-lip(pl.) · anything · utter(pst.) · with · which · her-soul(acc.) · she(sg.) · bind(pst.),
Analysis: if:cont she at all husband have:pa when she vow:pa or from her/lip:pl anything utter:pa with which her/soul:a she bind:pa,
Source conditional chronology retained without replacing it with a modern marriage contract model. Historical correction 281: clause-cont. Participant identities, polarity and quantities retained.

if(unmarked.continuation) · she(sg.) · in · of · her-husband · house · vow(pst.) · or · her-soul(acc.) · by · bond · with · oath · bind(pst.),
Analysis: if:cont she in of her/husband house vow:pa or her/soul:a by bond with oath bind:pa,
Second household formulation translated fully, not dropped as a duplicate. Historical correction 281: clause-cont. Participant identities, polarity and quantities retained.

from(unmarked.continuation) · of · Kedemoth · wilderness · to · Sihon · of · Heshbon · king · with · of · peace · word(pl.) · messenger(pl.,acc.) · I(sg.) · send(pst.) · say(cv.),
Analysis: from:cont of kjv_kedemoth kjv_wilderness to kjv_sihon of kjv_heshbon king with of peace word:pl messenger:pl:a i send:pa say:cv,
Moses individual sender introduces representative journey speech. Historical correction 281: clause-cont. Participant identities, polarity and quantities retained.

for · money · food(acc.) · to · I(pl.self.) · you(fam.sg.) · sell(fut.) · that · eat(prs.,abil.), · and · for · money · water(acc.) · to · I(pl.self.) · give(imp.) · that · drink(prs.,abil.). · only · on · my(pl.self.)-foot(pl.) · through · I(pl.self.) · pass(fut.),
Analysis: for money food:a to ipl thou sell:fu that eat:pr:can, and for money water:a to ipl give:imp that drink:pr:can. only on mypl/foot:pl through ipl pass:fu,
Paid passage retained, corporate speaker changes back to singular-we in the next possessive clause.

for · thyself · any · graven · image · or · any · of · anything · likeness · that · in · heaven · above · or · earth · beneath · or · water(pl.) · beneath · earth · be(prs.) · you(fam.sg.) · make(fut.) · not,
Analysis: for thyself any kjv_graven image or any of anything likeness that in heaven above or earth beneath or water:pl beneath earth be:pr thou make:fu not,
